{"file":"Skills For Real Engineers-1.2.3-v1.zip","bytes":309350,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"mattpocock-skills","description":"Matt Pocock's agent skills for real engineering: grilling, spec/ticket flows, TDD, code review, domain modelling and more. Plug-and-play, not vibe coding.","version":"1.2.3","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/mattpocock/skills","homepage":"https://www.aihero.dev/s/skills-newsletter","keywords":["engineering","skills","tdd","code-review","grilling","domain-modeling","productivity"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/engineering/ask-matt/SKILL.md","name":"ask-matt","description":"Ask which skill or flow fits your situation. A router over the skills in this repo.","headings":["Ask Matt","The main flow: idea → ship","Context hygiene","On-ramps","Codebase health","Vocabulary underneath","Phase boundaries","Standalone","Precondition"],"name_hint":"ask · matt","description_zh":"根据用户情况，在该仓库的技能和流程之间选择合适入口。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/code-review/SKILL.md","name":"code-review","description":"Review the changes since a fixed point (commit, branch, tag, or merge-base) along two axes: Standards (does the code follow this repo's documented coding standards?) and Spec (does the code match what the originating issue/spec asked for?). Runs both reviews in parallel sub-agents and reports them side by side. Use when the user wants to review a branch, a PR, work-in-progress changes, or asks to \"review since X\".","headings":["Process","1. Pin the fixed point","2. Identify the spec source","3. Identify the standards sources","4. Spawn both sub-agents in parallel","5. Aggregate","Why two axes"],"name_hint":"代码 · 评审","description_zh":"从指定提交、分支、标签或 merge-base 起审查变化，分别检查仓库编码标准与原始 issue/规格的一致性，通过并行子智能体执行两项审查并并列报告。适用于分支、PR、进行中工作或指定起点的评审。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/codebase-design/SKILL.md","name":"codebase-design","description":"Shared vocabulary for designing deep modules. Use when the user wants to design or improve a module's interface, find deepening opportunities, decide where a seam goes, make code more testable or AI-navigable, or when another skill needs the deep-module vocabulary.","headings":["Codebase Design","Glossary","Deep vs shallow","Principles","Designing for testability","Relationships","Rejected framings","Going deeper"],"name_hint":"codebase · 设计","description_zh":"提供深层模块设计的共享术语，适用于接口设计、模块深化、边界选择、可测试性及 AI 导航改善，也供其他技能引用。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/diagnosing-bugs/SKILL.md","name":"diagnosing-bugs","description":"Diagnosis loop for hard bugs and performance regressions. Use when the user says \"diagnose\"/\"debug this\", or reports something broken/throwing/failing/slow.","headings":["Diagnosing Bugs","Redact","Phase 1: Build a feedback loop","Ways to construct one, in roughly this order","Tighten the loop","Non-deterministic bugs","When you genuinely cannot build a loop","Completion criterion: a tight loop that goes red","Phase 2: Reproduce + minimise","Minimise","Phase 3: Hypothesise","Phase 4: Instrument","Phase 5: Fix + regression test","Phase 6: Cleanup"],"name_hint":"diagnosing · bugs","description_zh":"对难定位的缺陷或性能退化开展循环诊断，分析报错、失败和运行缓慢等问题。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/domain-modeling/SKILL.md","name":"domain-modeling","description":"Build and sharpen a project's domain model. Use when discussing codebase terminology, writing or editing a CONTEXT.md, or recording or editing an ADR.","headings":["Domain Modeling","File structure","During the session","Challenge against the glossary","Sharpen fuzzy language","Discuss concrete scenarios","Cross-reference with code","Update CONTEXT.md inline","Offer ADRs sparingly"],"name_hint":"domain · modeling","description_zh":"建立并完善项目领域模型，适用于代码库术语讨论、CONTEXT.md 编写修改及 ADR 记录维护。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/grill-with-docs/SKILL.md","name":"grill-with-docs","description":"A relentless interview to sharpen a plan or design, which also creates docs (ADR's and glossary) as we go.","headings":[],"name_hint":"grill · with · 文档","description_zh":"通过持续追问澄清并完善计划或设计，同时逐步生成 ADR 和术语表。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/implement/SKILL.md","name":"implement","description":"Implement a piece of work based on a spec or set of tickets.","headings":[],"name_hint":"implement","description_zh":"依据规格或工单集合实现具体工作。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/improve-codebase-architecture/SKILL.md","name":"improve-codebase-architecture","description":"Scan a codebase for deepening opportunities, present them as a visual HTML report, then grill through whichever one you pick.","headings":["Improve Codebase Architecture","Process","1. Explore","2. Present candidates as an HTML report","3. Grilling loop"],"name_hint":"improve · codebase · architecture","description_zh":"扫描代码库中可进一步改善设计的机会，生成可视化 HTML 报告，并深入讨论用户选中的方案。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/prototype/SKILL.md","name":"prototype","description":"Build a throwaway prototype to answer a design question. Use when the user wants to sanity-check whether a state model or logic feels right, or explore what a UI should look like.","headings":["Prototype","Pick a branch","Rules that apply to both"],"name_hint":"prototype","description_zh":"构建可丢弃的原型，验证状态模型、逻辑或界面设计是否符合预期。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/research/SKILL.md","name":"research","description":"Investigate a question against high-trust primary sources and capture the findings as a Markdown file in the repo. Use when the user wants a topic researched, docs or API facts gathered, or reading legwork delegated to a background agent.","headings":[],"name_hint":"研究","description_zh":"依据可信一手资料研究问题，核对文档及 API 事实，并将发现保存为仓库中的 Markdown 文件。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/resolving-merge-conflicts/SKILL.md","name":"resolving-merge-conflicts","description":"Use when you need to resolve an in-progress git merge/rebase conflict.","headings":[],"name_hint":"resolving · 合并 · conflicts","description_zh":"解决正在进行中的 Git merge 或 rebase 冲突。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/setup-matt-pocock-skills/SKILL.md","name":"setup-matt-pocock-skills","description":"Configure this repo for the engineering skills: set up its issue tracker, triage label vocabulary, and domain doc layout. Run once before first use of the other engineering skills.","headings":["Setup Matt Pocock's Skills","Process","1. Explore","2. Present findings and ask","3. Confirm and edit","4. Write","Agent skills","Issue tracker","Triage labels","Domain docs","5. Done"],"name_hint":"设置 · matt · pocock · 技能","description_zh":"首次使用工程技能前配置仓库的议题跟踪系统、分类标签词汇及领域文档布局。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/tdd/SKILL.md","name":"tdd","description":"Test-driven development. Use when the user wants to build features or fix bugs test-first, mentions \"red-green-refactor\", or wants integration tests.","headings":["Test-Driven Development","What a good test is","Seams: where tests go","Anti-patterns","Rules of the loop"],"name_hint":"tdd","description_zh":"采用测试驱动开发实现功能或修复缺陷，通过红灯、绿灯、重构步骤推进，也用于集成测试。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/to-spec/SKILL.md","name":"to-spec","description":"Turn the current conversation into a spec and publish it to the project issue tracker: no interview, just synthesis of what you've already discussed.","headings":["Process","Problem Statement","Solution","User Stories","Implementation Decisions","Testing Decisions","Out of Scope","Further Notes"],"name_hint":"to · spec","description_zh":"直接综合当前会话中已讨论的信息形成规格，并发布到项目议题跟踪系统。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/to-tickets/SKILL.md","name":"to-tickets","description":"Break a plan, spec, or the current conversation into a set of tracer-bullet tickets, each declaring its blocking edges, published to the configured tracker (edges as text in one file per ticket locally, or native blocking links on a real tracker).","headings":["To Tickets","Process","1. Gather context","2. Explore the codebase (optional)","3. Draft vertical slices","4. Quiz the user","5. Publish the tickets to the configured tracker","<NN>: <Ticket title>","Parent","What to build","Acceptance criteria","Blocked by"],"name_hint":"to · tickets","description_zh":"将计划、规格或当前讨论拆成可逐步验证端到端路径的工单，声明阻塞依赖，并以本地文件或跟踪系统原生关系记录。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/triage/SKILL.md","name":"triage","description":"Move issues and external PRs through a state machine of triage roles, categorise, verify, grill if needed, and write agent-ready briefs.","headings":["Triage","Reference docs","Roles","Invocation","Show what needs attention","Triage a specific issue or PR","Quick state override","Needs-info template","Triage Notes","Resuming a previous session"],"name_hint":"triage","description_zh":"按分类角色状态机处理议题与外部 PR，完成分类、核验和必要的深入询问，形成可供代理执行的简报。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/wayfinder/SKILL.md","name":"wayfinder","description":"Plan a huge chunk of work (more than one agent session can hold) as a shared map of decision tickets on your issue tracker, and resolve them one at a time until the way to the destination is clear.","headings":["Plan, don't do","Refer by name","The Map","The map body","Destination","Notes","Decisions so far","Not yet specified","Out of scope","Tickets","Question","Ticket Types","Fog of war","Out of scope","Invocation","Chart the map","Work through the map"],"name_hint":"wayfinder","description_zh":"将超出单次代理会话容量的大型工作规划为议题系统中的共享决策地图，逐一解决决策工单以明确实施路径。"},{"path":"skills/engineering/wizard/SKILL.md","name":"wizard","description":"Generate an interactive bash wizard that walks a human through steps only they can perform. Use when provisioning infrastructure, setting up credentials or CI secrets, walking an unfamiliar third-party dashboard, or running a one-off migration or cutover. Don't invoke this for steps the agent can perform itself.","headings":["Wizard","Process","1. Scope the procedure","2. Map each stage's journey","3. Author the wizard","4. Verify and hand off"],"name_hint":"wizard","description_zh":"生成交互式 Bash 向导，指导人工完成只有本人能执行的基础设施配置、凭据或 CI 密钥设置、陌生第三方控制台操作、一次性迁移及切换。智能体能自行完成的步骤不使用本项。"},{"path":"skills/in-progress/claude-handoff/SKILL.md","name":"claude-handoff","description":"Hand the current conversation off to a fresh background agent that picks up the work immediately.","headings":[],"name_hint":"claude · 交接","description_zh":"将当前对话交接给新的后台智能体，由其立即继续工作。"},{"path":"skills/in-progress/implement-spec/SKILL.md","name":"implement-spec","description":"Implement a specification in code.","headings":["Steps"],"name_hint":"implement · spec","description_zh":"依据规格编写实现代码。"},{"path":"skills/in-progress/loop-me/SKILL.md","name":"loop-me","description":"Grill me about specs for the workflows I want to build, within this workspace.","headings":["The loop lens","Vocabulary","Definition of done","The workspace"],"name_hint":"loop · me","description_zh":"在当前工作区通过追问明确用户希望构建的工作流规格。"},{"path":"skills/in-progress/pr/SKILL.md","name":"pr","description":"Use when writing a PR body.","headings":["Summary","Evidence","Merge Danger","Sections","Summary","Evidence","Merge Danger"],"name_hint":"pr","description_zh":"撰写 PR 正文。"},{"path":"skills/in-progress/retro/SKILL.md","name":"retro","description":"Conduct a retrospective on a coding session.","headings":["Steps","Reference","Implementation vs Review","Files"],"name_hint":"retro","description_zh":"对一次编码会话进行复盘。"},{"path":"skills/in-progress/setup-ts-deep-modules/SKILL.md","name":"setup-ts-deep-modules","description":"Wire dependency-cruiser into a TypeScript repo so each package is a deep module, with implementation hidden in subfolders and reachable only through its entry-point files. User-invoked.","headings":["Setup TS Deep Modules","The shape this enforces","Steps","1. Detect the environment","2. Install dependency-cruiser","3. Write the config","4. Wire it into the checks","5. Scaffold the example package","6. Prove the rules bite","7. Document the convention","Notes"],"name_hint":"设置 · ts · deep · modules","description_zh":"在用户调用时为 TypeScript 仓库接入 dependency-cruiser，将各包组织为深层模块，把实现隐藏于子目录并仅允许通过入口文件访问。"},{"path":"skills/in-progress/writing-beats/SKILL.md","name":"writing-beats","description":"Writing, exploit; assemble raw material into a journey of beats, grounding each term before a beat leans on it.","headings":["Grounding","What is a beat","Pulling from the pile","Ending the journey","Writing rhythm"],"name_hint":"writing · beats","description_zh":"将写作原始素材组织为连续的叙事节拍，在后续节拍引用术语前先解释其含义。"},{"path":"skills/in-progress/writing-fragments/SKILL.md","name":"writing-fragments","description":"Writing, explore: mine raw fragments, no structure yet.","headings":["What is a fragment","File format","Working title","Writing rhythm"],"name_hint":"writing · fragments","description_zh":"在写作探索阶段发掘原始片段，暂不组织结构。"},{"path":"skills/in-progress/writing-shape/SKILL.md","name":"writing-shape","description":"Writing, exploit: shape raw material into an article, paragraph by paragraph.","headings":["The loop","Grounding","Conversational feel","Pulling from the pile","Format arguments to actually have","Writing rhythm","Out of scope"],"name_hint":"writing · shape","description_zh":"在写作成形阶段逐段将原始素材塑造成文章。"},{"path":"skills/misc/git-guardrails-claude-code/SKILL.md","name":"git-guardrails-claude-code","description":"Set up Claude Code hooks to block dangerous git commands (push, reset --hard, clean, branch -D, etc.) before they execute. Use when user wants to prevent destructive git operations, add git safety hooks, or block git push/reset in Claude Code.","headings":["Setup Git Guardrails","What Gets Blocked","Steps","1. Ask scope","2. Copy the hook script","3. Add hook to settings","4. Ask about customization","5. Verify"],"name_hint":"Git · guardrails · claude · 代码","description_zh":"为 Claude Code 配置执行前的 Git 安全钩子，阻止 push、reset --hard、clean、强制删分支等指定命令。"},{"path":"skills/misc/migrate-to-shoehorn/SKILL.md","name":"migrate-to-shoehorn","description":"Migrate test files from `as` type assertions to @total-typescript/shoehorn. Use when user mentions shoehorn, wants to replace `as` in tests, or needs partial test data.","headings":["Migrate to Shoehorn","Why shoehorn?","Install","Migration patterns","Large objects with few needed properties","`as Type` → `fromPartial()`","`as unknown as Type` → `fromAny()`","When to use each","Workflow"],"name_hint":"migrate · to · shoehorn","description_zh":"将测试中的 as 类型断言迁移为 @total-typescript/shoehorn，并支持构造部分测试数据。"},{"path":"skills/misc/scaffold-exercises/SKILL.md","name":"scaffold-exercises","description":"Create exercise directory structures with sections, problems, solutions, and explainers that pass linting. Use when user wants to scaffold exercises, create exercise stubs, or set up a new course section.","headings":["Scaffold Exercises","Directory naming","Exercise variants","Required files","Exercise Title","Workflow","Lint rules summary","Moving/renaming exercises","Example: stubbing from a plan"],"name_hint":"scaffold · exercises","description_zh":"搭建课程练习目录，包含章节、题目、答案和讲解，确保结构通过 lint 检查。"},{"path":"skills/misc/setup-pre-commit/SKILL.md","name":"setup-pre-commit","description":"Set up Husky pre-commit hooks with lint-staged (Prettier), type checking, and tests in the current repo. Use when user wants to add pre-commit hooks, set up Husky, configure lint-staged, or add commit-time formatting/typechecking/testing.","headings":["Setup Pre-Commit Hooks","What This Sets Up","Steps","1. Detect package manager","2. Install dependencies","3. Initialize Husky","4. Create `.husky/pre-commit`","5. Create `.lintstagedrc`","6. Create `.prettierrc` (if missing)","7. Verify","8. Commit","Notes"],"name_hint":"设置 · pre · 提交","description_zh":"为仓库配置 Husky 提交前钩子，结合 lint-staged/Prettier、类型检查和测试，在提交时自动验证与格式化。"},{"path":"skills/productivity/grill-me/SKILL.md","name":"grill-me","description":"A relentless interview to sharpen a plan or design.","headings":[],"name_hint":"grill · me","description_zh":"通过持续深入提问，澄清和完善计划或设计。"},{"path":"skills/productivity/grilling/SKILL.md","name":"grilling","description":"Grill the user relentlessly about a plan, decision, or idea. Use when the user wants to stress-test their thinking, or uses any 'grill' trigger phrases.","headings":[],"name_hint":"grilling","description_zh":"对计划、决策或创意持续追问，适用于用户希望检验思考的稳健性或要求深入质询。"},{"path":"skills/productivity/handoff/SKILL.md","name":"handoff","description":"Compact the current conversation into a handoff document for another agent to pick up.","headings":[],"name_hint":"交接","description_zh":"将当前对话压缩成供其他智能体接续的交接文档。"},{"path":"skills/productivity/teach/SKILL.md","name":"teach","description":"Teach the user a new skill or concept, within this workspace.","headings":["Teaching Workspace","Philosophy","Fluency vs Storage Strength","Lessons","Assets","The Mission","Zone Of Proximal Development","Knowledge","Skills","Acquiring Wisdom","Reference Documents","`NOTES.md`"],"name_hint":"teach","description_zh":"在当前工作区内教授用户新的技能或概念。"},{"path":"skills/productivity/to-questionnaire/SKILL.md","name":"to-questionnaire","description":"Turn a decision you can't fully answer into a questionnaire for someone else to fill in.","headings":["Document structure","<Questionnaire title>","Context","How to answer","<Theme heading>","What load is the system expected to handle at launch?","Anything else?"],"name_hint":"to · questionnaire","description_zh":"将尚无法完整回答的决策问题整理为供其他人填写的问卷。"},{"path":"skills/productivity/wait-what/SKILL.md","name":"wait-what","description":"Stop. That last message did not land: re-pitch it.","headings":[],"name_hint":"wait · what","description_zh":"重新组织上一条未能有效传达的消息，使表达更贴合接收者。"},{"path":"skills/productivity/writing-for-agents/SKILL.md","name":"writing-for-agents","description":"Writing documents for agents. Use when creating or editing skills, or modifying AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md.","headings":["Context pointers","The two loads","Information hierarchy","Steps and completion criteria","When to split","Leading words","Pruning"],"name_hint":"writing · for · 智能体","description_zh":"为智能体编写文档，适用于技能创建编辑及 AGENTS.md、CLAUDE.md 修改。"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Skills For Real Engineers","Installation (30-second setup)","1. Get the skills","2. Run `/setup-matt-pocock-skill